

FAE — Unified API Specification (Atomic‑Gradient Propulsion System)

C. Matthew Blackwell — Conceptual System Architecture

⭐ 1. System Identity

System Name: First Atoms Engine (FAE)

Domain: Atomic‑state propulsion simulation

Core Principle: Motion emerges from engineered atomic energy‑density gradients

Architecture: Multi‑layer field construction → gradient solving → entropy reinforcement → drift evaluation

Constraint:[ v_{eff} < c ]

⭐ 2. Global Data Structures

2.1 EnvState

Represents external astrophysical and environmental atomic inputs.

C(t) — cosmic telemetry

S(t, λ) — spectral density

Z_env — atomic composition of environment

2.2 AnchorState

Represents internal fusion‑anchor and confinement state.

F_PtU(t) — Pt/U fusion state vector

M_conf(t) — MHD confinement parameters

Psi_core(t) — coherence of fusion anchor

2.3 FieldState

Represents atomic stability fields and gradients.

Phi_ext(t, x) — external atomic stability field

Phi_int(t, x) — internal atomic anchor field

GradPhi(t, x) — raw gradient

GradPhi_star(t, x) — entropy‑reinforced gradient

2.4 EntropyState

Represents atomic‑scale entropy dynamics.

E_spike(t) — fusion energy spike

S_A(t) — atomic entropy term

2.5 DriftState

Represents motion output.

v_eff(t, x) — drift velocity

a_eff(t, x) — drift acceleration

⭐ 3. Module APIs

3.1 Environment Ingest Module

Function: ingest_environment()Input: cosmic telemetry, spectral data, Z_envOutput: EnvStatePurpose: Normalize astrophysical inputs into usable atomic‑field parameters.

3.2 Fusion Anchor Module

Function: ingest_anchor()Input: fusion diagnostics, MHD parameters, coherence metricsOutput: AnchorStatePurpose: Encode Pt/U fusion anchor and confinement state.

3.3 Field Construction Module

Function: build_fields(env, anchor)Input: EnvState, AnchorStateOutput: FieldStatePurpose: Construct external and internal atomic stability fields.

3.4 Gradient Solver Module

Function: solve_gradient(fields)Input: FieldStateOutput: updated FieldStatePurpose: Compute atomic stability gradient using:

MHD stability

Coulomb‑barrier modulation

atomic flux–velocity coupling

3.5 Entropy Reinforcement Module

Function: compute_entropy(anchor)Input: AnchorStateOutput: EntropyStatePurpose: Detect fusion spikes → convert to atomic entropy.

Function: reinforce_gradient(fields, entropy)Input: FieldState, EntropyStateOutput: updated FieldStatePurpose: Deepen gradient using entropy reinforcement.

3.6 Drift Evaluation Module

Function: evaluate_drift(fields, entropy)Input: FieldState, EntropyStateOutput: DriftStatePurpose: Compute drift velocity and acceleration under relativistic constraint.

⭐ 4. Motion Law (Expanded)

[ v_{eff} = k_{A} \cdot |\nabla \Phi_{A}^{*}| \cdot S_{A} ]

Acceleration:

[ a_{eff} = \frac{\partial v_{eff}}{\partial t} ]

Relativistic correction:

[ v_{eff} < c ]

Gradient direction:

[ \hat{n}{\Phi} = \frac{\nabla \Phi{A}^{}}{|\nabla \Phi_{A}^{}|} ]

Trajectory:

[ \frac{d\mathbf{r}}{dt} = v_{eff} \hat{n}_{\Phi} ]

⭐ 5. Kernel Orchestration

Function: run_fae_step(t)

Executes one full simulation step.

Flow:

ingest_environment()

ingest_anchor()

build_fields()

solve_gradient()

compute_entropy()

reinforce_gradient()

evaluate_drift()

Output:EnvState, AnchorState, FieldState, EntropyState, DriftState

Function: run_fae_simulation(t_start, t_end, dt)

Runs full simulation across time window.

Output:Time series of FieldState + DriftState

⭐ 6. Logging API

Function: log_state(t, EnvState, AnchorState, FieldState, EntropyState, DriftState)Stores full atomic‑field and drift history.

